{
    "background_story": "Olivia was a brilliant and ambitious archaeologist, renowned for her groundbreaking research on ancient civilizations. Her life's passion was uncovering the secrets of the Code of Hammurabi, one of the earliest surviving codes of law. Olivia spent years studying the cuneiform script, pouring over ancient texts and scouring the deserts of Mesopotamia for clues. Her tireless efforts paid off when she discovered a long-lost tablet fragment that shed new light on the code's origins. As she carefully translated the text, Olivia became increasingly fascinated by the code's emphasis on fairness, justice, and the protection of the weak. She saw parallels between Hammurabi's vision and her own desire to use her knowledge to make a positive impact on the world. Olivia's work sparked a new wave of interest in ancient law and its relevance to modern society.",
